<gpx creator="StravaGPX" version="1.1" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
 <metadata>
  <name>NETHERLANDS - AMSTERDAM - KOM OP GERRIE ! (*)</name>
  <desc>Gerrie Knetemann was a Dutch cycling star of the seventies and eighties, a stalwart of the legendary TI–Raleigh team, and a multiple Yellow Jersey wearer. Born in Amsterdam, he died in 2004. An annual Gran Fondo race is staged in his honor, exploring those parks, polders, and cycle paths to the south of the capital.

Gerrie Knetemann était une figure des années 1970-1980, pilier de la mythique TI-Raleigh, multiple maillot jaune. Chaque été, un Gran Fondo rend hommage à ce natif d’Amsterdam, décédé en 2004, en explorant parcs, canaux, polders et des dizaines de km de voies cyclables au sud de la ville. On s’en inspire largement ici,

. This route was published, detailed and filled inside Cycling Atlas Europe, The 350 most beautiful cycling routes in Old Continent provided by Strava, by Claude Droussent (Universe Publishing in EN - 2023). In other languages: L’Atlas Vélo Europe (Solar Éditions FR), Ciclo Atlante d’Europa ( Touring Club Italiano IT).

(*) Come on Geerie ! in Dutch. 
</desc>
  <author>
   <name>Andrew Goudie</name>
  </author>
  <copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors">
   <year>2020</year>
   <license>https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright</license>
  </copyright>
 </metadata>
